//
// HAND-WRITTEN: an address from %tid.x through 300 additions of 1, one
// definition each, longer than a trace follows in one recursion
// (DEPTH_LIMIT, 32): a query traces first, on its own, each value its
// trace was cut at, so the address reads 4 * %tid.x + param_0 + 1200
// whatever was read before it. The second kernel's loop compares its
// counter with 40, reached through 40 additions of 1, and so counts
// 40 trips.
//
.version 8.7
.target sm_89
.address_size 64

